# Adding a New Agent to Pocketknife

This guide outlines the complete process for adding a new agent to the Pocketknife platform. Follow this checklist to ensure consistency across all agents.

## Quick Checklist

| Step | Backend | Frontend | Database |
|:---:|:---|:---|:---|
| 1 | ☐ Prisma Schema | ☐ Types | ☐ Models |
| 2 | ☐ Service | ☐ API Service | - |
| 3 | ☐ Agent Class | ☐ Hook | - |
| 4 | ☐ Controller | ☐ Component | - |
| 5 | ☐ Routes | ☐ App.tsx Tab | - |
| 6 | ☐ Config Entries | ☐ Styles | - |
| 7 | ☐ Register Agent | - | - |

---

## Step 1: Database Schema (Prisma)

### File: `backend/prisma/schema.prisma`

Add your models at the end of the file:

```prisma
// =============================================================================
// YOUR_AGENT_NAME AGENT
// =============================================================================

model YourModel {
  id        String   @id @default(uuid())
  userId    String
  user      User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  
  // Your fields here
  name      String
  status    String   @default("active")
  
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([userId])
}
```

### Add User Relations

In the `User` model, add your agent's relations:

```prisma
model User {
  // ... existing relations ...
  
  // YourAgent relations
  yourModels    YourModel[]
}
```

### Run Migration

```bash
cd backend && npx prisma migrate dev --name add_your_agent
```

