## Step 6: Configuration (Three-Tier System)

Your agent should use the dynamic configuration system. See `.cursor/rules/dynamic-configuration.mdc` for full details.

### 6a. Config Service (Simple Values)

File: `backend/src/services/core/configService.ts`

Add your agent's config entries in `DEFAULT_CONFIG`:

```typescript
const DEFAULT_CONFIG = {
  // ... existing config ...

  // ==========================================================================
  // YOUR AGENT
  // ==========================================================================
  'yourAgent.maxResults': 20,
  'yourAgent.cacheMinutes': 30,
  'yourAgent.ai.maxTokens': 2000,
  'yourAgent.api.timeoutMs': 10000,
  'yourAgent.feature.enabled': true,
} as const;
```

### 6b. Using Config in Your Agent

```typescript
// In your agent or service
import { configService } from '../services/core/configService';

const maxResults = configService.get('yourAgent.maxResults', 20);
const aiTokens = configService.get('yourAgent.ai.maxTokens', 2000);
```

### 6c. Business Rules (Optional)

If your agent has complex conditional logic (scoring, filtering), use the Rule Engine:

```typescript
import { ruleEngineService, RuleContext } from '../services/rules';

const context: RuleContext = {
  agentId: 'your-agent',
  action: 'score-item',
  data: { price: item.price, category: item.category }
};

const result = await ruleEngineService.evaluate(context, 'scoring');
const score = result.finalContext.data.score;
```

### 6d. Feature Flags (Optional)

For feature toggles or A/B tests:

```typescript
import { featureFlagService } from '../services/featureFlags';

if (await featureFlagService.isEnabled('yourAgent.newAlgorithm')) {
  // New implementation
}
```

